Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and why they matter  
• state : state abbreviation – the field we have to rank and finally report.  
• event_id : unique id of each storm event – counting these (COUNT(*)) gives the number of events.  
• event_begin_time : contains the date → in case we need to double‑check the year, but each table already holds one calendar year.  

Main filter / conditions  
• Year has to be between 1980 and 1995 (tables storms_1980 … storms_1995).  
• Inside every year keep only the 1 000 states that have the largest event counts (RANK() ≤ 1000).  
• Aggregate those “kept” counts over the whole 1980‑1995 period and pick the 5 states with the biggest total.  

Below are ten progressively more complex queries that explore the data and finally answer the question.  
(Every query finishes with LIMIT 20 as requested.)

```sql
-- 1. Peek at a few raw rows from 1980
SELECT state, event_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_historic_severe_storms.storms_1980`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Distinct state abbreviations that appear in 1980
SELECT DISTINCT UPPER(state) AS state_abbr
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_historic_severe_storms.storms_1980`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Count events per state in 1980
SELECT UPPER(state) AS state_abbr,
       COUNT(*) AS events_1980
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_historic_severe_storms.storms_1980`
GROUP BY state_abbr
ORDER BY events_1980 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Top 10 states by event count in 1983
SELECT state_abbr, events_1983
FROM (
  SELECT UPPER(state) AS state_abbr,
         COUNT(*) AS events_1983,
         RANK() OVER(ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) AS rnk
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_historic_severe_storms.storms_1983`
  GROUP BY state_abbr
)
WHERE rnk <= 10
ORDER BY events_1983 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Combine every table 1980‑1995, tagging the year
SELECT 1980 AS yr, state FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_historic_severe_storms.storms_1980`
UNION ALL
SELECT 1981 AS yr, state FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_historic_severe_storms.storms_1981`
UNION ALL
